course: dictionary
lesson: 12560
title: Diagnosis: finding the cause
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diagnosis is the decision someone makes about what is wrong, after they look at the signs. A doctor looks at your spots, your temperature and how you feel, and then makes a diagnosis. «The doctor listened to Sam's chest and made a diagnosis: he had a chest infection.»
explain: The word is not only for people. A mechanic can make a diagnosis of a car when it will not start. They plug in a computer, check the parts and find the fault. «The diagnosis was a flat battery.»
explain: Read the words around diagnosis to understand it. Words like doctor, signs, checked, tests and fault are clues. Ask yourself: has someone found the cause of a problem? If yes, the word is probably diagnosis.
fact: A diagnosis is a noun. Its plural is diagnoses.
fact: In medicine, a diagnosis is the doctor's decision about what illness or problem someone has.
fact: A diagnosis can also mean finding out what is wrong with a machine, a car or a system.
fact: «An early diagnosis» means the problem was found near the start, when it was first noticed.
fact: To diagnose is the verb: a doctor or mechanic can diagnose a problem.
exercise: «The doctor checked Sam and gave his diagnosis.» What is a diagnosis? | A kind of medicine | A hospital bed | *The doctor's decision about what is wrong | The bill for the visit
exercise: «The mechanic plugged a computer into the car to get a diagnosis.» What is the diagnosis for? | Painting the car a new colour | Washing the car | Choosing a new car | *Finding out what is wrong with the car
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the decision about what is wrong. «The diagnosis was a broken arm.» | broken | arm | *diagnosis | doctor
test: «Mia had an early diagnosis, so her treatment could start sooner.» What does early diagnosis mean? | A diagnosis that happens last | A diagnosis that is wrong | A diagnosis made in the morning only | *Finding the problem near the start
test: Which sentence uses the word diagnosis correctly? | *The doctor made a diagnosis after looking at the signs | I went to the diagnosis to buy sweets | The bike had a new bell, which was its diagnosis | Her diagnosis was a ten-mile run
exam: Which is the plural of diagnosis? | diagnosisies | *diagnoses | diagnosises | diagnosiss
